{"key":"enterprise/T1489","id":"T1489","name":"Service Stop","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["impact"],"platforms":["ESXi","IaaS","Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may stop or disable services on a system to render those services unavailable to legitimate users. Stopping critical services or processes can inhibit or stop response to an incident or aid in the adversary's overall objectives to cause damage to the environment. Adversaries may accomplish this by disabling individual services of high importance to an organization, such as MSExchangeIS, which will make Exchange content inaccessible.…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1489","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--20fb2507-d71c-455d-9b6d-6104461cf26b","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.622Z","source_object_version":"1.4","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0040","name":"File Deletion","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0040","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--e905dad2-00d6-477c-97e8-800427abd0e8","page":"telemetry/DC0040/"},{"id":"DC0088","name":"Logon Session Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0088","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--39b9db72-8b48-4595-a18d-db5bbba3091b","page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0033","name":"Process Termination","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0033","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--61f1d40e-f3d0-4cc6-aa2d-937b6204194f","page":"telemetry/DC0033/"},{"id":"DC0060","name":"Service Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0060","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5297a638-1382-4f0c-8472-0d21830bf705","page":"telemetry/DC0060/"},{"id":"DC0041","name":"Service Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0041","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--74fa567d-bc90-425c-8a41-3c703abb221c","page":"telemetry/DC0041/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0021","name":"Behavioral Detection for Service Stop across Platforms","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--ae37afa8-87d5-4091-ac33-010e78eefe97","relationship_id":"relationship--091187a1-a960-4731-829d-de865e7d49a1"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0061","name":"Analytic 0061","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0061","guidance":"Adversary disables or stops critical services (e.g., Exchange, SQL, AV, endpoint monitoring) using native utilities or API calls, often preceding destructive actions (T1485, T1486). Behavioral chain: Elevated execution context + stop-service or sc.exe or ChangeServiceConfigW + terminated or disabled service + possible follow-up file manipulation.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0021"},{"id":"AN0062","name":"Analytic 0062","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0062","guidance":"Adversary executes systemctl or service stop targeting high-value services (e.g., mysql, sshd), possibly followed by rm or shred against data stores. Behavioral chain: sudo/su usage + stop command + /var/log/messages or syslog entries + file access/delete.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0021"},{"id":"AN0063","name":"Analytic 0063","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0063","guidance":"Use of launchctl to stop services or kill critical background processes (e.g., securityd, com.apple.*), typically followed by command-line tools like rm or diskutil. Behavioral chain: Terminal or remote shell + launchctl bootout/disable + process termination + follow-on modification.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0021"},{"id":"AN0064","name":"Analytic 0064","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0064","guidance":"Attacker disables VM-related services or stops VMs forcibly to target vmdk or logs. Behavioral chain: esxcli or vim-cmd stop + audit log showing user privilege use + datastore file manipulation.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0021"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0061","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0061","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0088","component":"Logon Session Metadata","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4672","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0061","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0061","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"component_id":"DC0060","component":"Service Creation","name":"WinEventLog:System","channel":"EventCode=7036","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0061","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0061","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0060/"},{"component_id":"DC0041","component":"Service Metadata","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=4","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0061","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0061","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0041/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"execve of systemctl or service stop","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0062","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0021#AN0062","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0040",